---
functor: 1
title: Text and punctuation
---

set heading(numbering: none)

A paragraph is lines of text with an empty line before and after it. Functor sets each paragraph itself: it shapes words with the font, hyphenates them with TeX patterns, and picks the line breaks for the whole paragraph.

# Inline marks

| Write | Result |
|:--|:--|
| `*italic*` or `_italic_` | *italic* |
| `**bold**` or `__bold__` | **bold** |
| a word between two backticks | `code` |
| `$x.hat$` | inline math: $x.hat$ |
| `[Functor](https://eleadlau-commits.github.io/Functor/)` | [Functor](https://eleadlau-commits.github.io/Functor/) |
| `![A plot](plot.svg)` | an image |
| `[@knuth84]` or `[@a; @b]` | a citation: [@knuth84] |
| `{n}` | the value of `let n = 3` |
| `claim.^[A note.]` | a numbered margin note |

# Punctuation

Functor changes some signs to the correct typographic sign.

| Write | Result | Name |
|:--|:--|:--|
| `"text"` | "text" | double quotes |
| `'text'`, `don't` | 'text', don't | single quotes, apostrophe |
| `3--5` | 3--5 | en dash, for ranges |
| `yes---no` | yes---no | em dash |
| `Theorem~2` | Theorem~2 | a space that does not break |

# Margin notes

`^[...]` right after a word makes a numbered note. The note can hold math and marks.

```fn
Functor builds each glyph.^[A built glyph takes less than one millisecond, for example $nabla.circle$.] The cache keeps it.
```

In the `quiet` style the note sits in the right margin, next to its line, and folds into the text on narrow screens. In the `classic` style it follows the paragraph.

# Plain signs

A backslash before a sign gives the plain sign.

| Write | Result |
|:--|:--|
| `\$` | a dollar sign |
| `\@` | an at sign |
| `\*`, `\_` | a star, an underscore |
| `\{` | a curly bracket |
| `\"`, `\'`, `\-`, `\~` | the plain quote, apostrophe, hyphen, tilde |

# Things to know

- A line that starts with a declaration word followed by a space is a declaration, for example `let n = 3`. Do not start a line of text with the lowercase words `object`, `sym`, `let`, `set`, `use`, `kind`, `style` or `default`.
- Math in text can break after `=`, `<` or `+`.
